title: The Rural Hinge
subtitle: [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": PSL is willing to negotiate—and unusually willing to threaten the cabinet.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": PSL is outside government: useful votes, rural reach, no cabinet veto.?]
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_rural_hinge_timer <= 0 and psl_seats > 0 and (psl_relation < 55 or ((ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl") and psl_coalition_dissent >= 15) or early_election_risk >= 30 or coalition_broken = 1)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_rural_hinge_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/cards/rural-hinge.webp

= The Rural Hinge

[? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": PSL sits
outside the cabinet. It may be useful on individual votes or indispensable to a
future majority, but it cannot make a current cultural bill a coalition
ultimatum. Its local governments still need clinics, buses and predictable
finance. ?]

[? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": PSL is the coalition's rural hinge and treats
every difficult vote as a fresh negotiation. Its local governments need
clinics, buses and predictable finance; its conservative wing is ready to
threaten the cabinet whenever the Left presses a cultural bill. ?]

- @material_channel
- @cultural_pause
- @draw_red_line

@material_channel
title: Build the relationship around clinics and municipal finance
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A useful material channel that carefully avoids values.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Joint municipal work requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; psl_relation += 7; local_network += 3; household_policy_pressure += 2; health_policy_pressure += 2; progressives_dissent += 3; spring_dissent += 2; rural_support += 3; pensioner_support += 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Inter-party opposition bargain"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left and PSL find a language of local services"

The meeting produces amendments on clinics, buses and county finance. It also
produces an agreement not to discuss abortion today. Everyone knows that
“today” cannot last through a coalition negotiation.

- #poland_card_finish

@cultural_pause
title: [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": Promise PSL a pause on cultural legislation?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": Offer opposition PSL a cultural truce?]
subtitle: [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl": The hinge is secured by handing it an early veto.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": Buy a parliamentary channel without pretending PSL can stop the cabinet.?]
on-arrival: {!
const support = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_support) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_support)
) / 3;
const salience = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_salience) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_salience)
) / 3;
const backlash = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_backlash) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_backlash)
) / 3;
const rightsRaw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const rightsNet = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, rightsRaw)
));
const net = -rightsNet;
Q.psl_relation += 9 + (net >= 1 ? 1 : 0);
Q.barons_dissent -= 3;
Q.party_unity += net >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.feminist_trust -= 5 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.progressive_credibility -= 3 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.progressives_dissent += 6 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.spring_dissent += 4 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.razem_dissent += 2 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.rural_support += Math.max(0, 2 + net);
Q.young_support -= 3 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.women_support -= 3 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.public_trust += net * 0.45;
for (const issue of [
    "abortion_rights",
    "lgbt_equality",
    "secular_state"
]) {
    Q[issue + "_salience"] -= 3;
    Q[issue + "_backlash"] -= net >= 0 ? 3 : 1;
}
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue =
    "Abortion, LGBT equality and secular institutions";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "PSL cultural pause";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "A cultural pause reassures a cautious electorate and PSL"
    : (net <= -1
        ? (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet || Q.government_party == "psl"
            ? "The PSL assurance is exposed as a veto over rights"
            : "The PSL assurance is exposed as a concession to the opposition")
        : "A quiet assurance buys louder rural cooperation");
!}

[? if (card_public_response = "breakthrough" or card_public_response =
"favourable") and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"):
Public opinion is more cautious than the movement. PSL's leadership stops
threatening to leave, and the pause buys support beyond the coalition room. ?]
[? if (card_public_response = "breakthrough" or card_public_response =
"favourable") and ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl":
Public opinion is more cautious than the movement. PSL opens a parliamentary
channel, but no cabinet threat has been withdrawn because none existed. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested" and ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and
government_party != "psl": PSL receives a programme concession from outside
government. Progressive MPs discover that the price of reassurance was paid
with their programme, not with cabinet stability. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested" and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl"): PSL's leadership withdraws its latest threat to
leave the cabinet. Progressive MPs discover that the price of reassurance was
paid with their programme. ?]
[? if (card_public_response = "backlash" or card_public_response = "reversal")
and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or government_party = "psl"): The electorate
has moved while the coalition bargain has not. What was meant to be quiet
reassurance becomes a visible conservative veto, and the Left pays for it among
women and younger voters. ?]
[? if (card_public_response = "backlash" or card_public_response = "reversal")
and ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": The electorate
has moved while Lewica is still paying an opposition party for reassurance.
The concession is visible; a PSL cabinet veto is not. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@draw_red_line
title: State that rights will not be coalition currency
subtitle: A clear principle strengthens the Left and may close the rural door.
on-arrival: {!
const support = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_support) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_support)
) / 3;
const salience = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_salience) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_salience)
) / 3;
const backlash = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_backlash) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_backlash)
) / 3;
const raw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.psl_relation -= 5 + Math.max(0, -net);
Q.feminist_trust += Math.max(2, Math.round(4 * scale));
Q.progressive_credibility += Math.max(2, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.spring_dissent -= 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
Q.party_unity -= net < 0 ? 2 : 1;
Q.public_trust += 1 + net * 0.40;
Q.women_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.young_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.rural_support -= net < 0 ? 2 : 1;
for (const issue of [
    "abortion_rights",
    "lgbt_equality",
    "secular_state"
]) {
    Q[issue + "_support"] += net >= 1 ? 1 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 0);
    Q[issue + "_salience"] += 4;
    Q[issue + "_backlash"] += net < 0 ? 4 : 2;
}
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue =
    "Abortion, LGBT equality and secular institutions";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Rights are not coalition currency";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "The Left finds public backing against a conservative veto"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The coalition red line triggers a public and rural backlash"
        : (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet || Q.government_party == "psl"
            ? "The Left refuses a conservative coalition veto"
            : "The Left refuses to buy opposition support with a rights pause"));
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough" and (ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl"): The declaration catches up with a public majority.
PSL calls it premature but discovers that its threatened veto is less popular
than the rights it would block. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough" and ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and
government_party != "psl": The declaration catches up with a public majority.
PSL can oppose it in the Sejm, but cannot present that opposition as a cabinet
veto. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": There will be compromise on
schedules and spending, but [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1 or
government_party = "psl": not a partner's veto over bodily autonomy.?][? if
ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0 and government_party != "psl": not a rights pause
bought from a party outside government.?] The organisers' red line has support
outside the room. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": PSL calls the declaration
premature. Your organisers call it overdue. Neither side can yet claim the
electorate as an answer. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": The principle strengthens the
movement and alarms a high-attention conservative electorate. The rural door
does not merely narrow; PSL threatens to close it. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": Rights remain a minority position in
an explosive climate. The red line is morally clear and electorally costly,
and every caucus knows both facts. ?]

- #poland_card_finish
